//@version=6
// CHoCH Setups (MES, MNQ, MYM, MGC)
// Shows graded BUY / SELL signals (A+, A, B) on a 1, 5 or 15-minute chart when the setup forms:
//   price pushes into a higher-timeframe swing level -> strong change of character on the chart's
//   candles -> limit entry at the fair-value gap it leaves.
// Every grade needs: a CHoCH candle that leaves a fair-value gap, at a higher-timeframe swing level, NOT at the
// previous day's high/low, in the direction of the higher-timeframe trend. The grade is how strong the CHoCH
// candle is vs the 30-candle average range (1M chart): A+ >= 1.5x, A 1.2x - 1.5x, B 1.0x - 1.2x.
// On 1M the push must be a real move INTO the level: the push candle's low (high for shorts) is also the lowest
// (highest) of the 15 candles before it. Without this, a selloff straight through a level counted as a push.
// Settings by chart timeframe (set automatically):
//   1M:  15M levels + 15M trend, touch within 1 pt, push within 20 bars, A+ / A / B
//   5M:  15M levels + 15M trend, touch within 3 pts, push within 6 bars, CHoCH body >= 1.0x (A+ only)
//   15M: 1H levels + 1H trend, touch within 4 pts, push within 4 bars, CHoCH body >= 1.0x (A+ only)
// Plan tested Sep 29 - Oct 28, 2026 on 1M (MES + MNQ + MYM as one group, MGC on its own, 2R, full exit):
//   signals 8:30 AM - 2:00 PM CT, A+ any time, A and B only after 11:00, first filled trade of the day,
//   limit cancelled after 10 candles, risk 10% of the balance: $1,000 -> $6,512 (26 trades, 18 wins).
//   Re-run it with tools/account_study.py. Sizing, fills and exits here work like that test: contracts = 10% of
//   the balance / loss per contract at the stop (rounded down, capped by day margin), a candle that opens past
//   the limit fills at its open, stops and 3:40 closes fill 1 tick worse, $1.24 commission per contract.
//   The test shared one first-trade-of-the-day across MES/MNQ/MYM; so does this ("One index trade a day" setting).
//   The 11:00 cutoff was picked after seeing the results (10:30 gave $2,356); "any time" gave $3,694.
//   1M was best; 5M made about half as much with deeper drawdowns; 15M about broke even.
// Each signal draws a position tool (green profit zone, red risk zone, like TradingView's Long / Short Position),
// the 15M level, the push, the CHoCH candle and entry / stop / target lines that follow the
// trade live (Filled, Target hit, Stopped). The label shows the stop and target in ticks, contracts for your risk, and the CHoCH candle's volume
// vs its 20-candle average. Volume was NOT part of the test - it is extra information only.
// Point settings are scaled to each market's candle size (MES/ES, MNQ/NQ, MYM/YM, MGC/GC, M2K/RTY).
// Levels and trend are only used for the signal and are not drawn.
// Only closed candles are used, so signals do not repaint. This never places orders.
indicator("CHoCH Setups", shorttitle="CHoCH A+/A/B", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_boxes_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_bars_back=200)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- per-timeframe settings
tfSec = timeframe.in_seconds()
tfIdx = tfSec < 300 ? 0 : tfSec < 900 ? 1 : 2      // 0 = 1M, 1 = 5M, 2 = 15M
htf   = tfIdx == 2 ? "60" : "15"                   // timeframe for levels and trend
htfTxt = tfIdx == 2 ? "1H" : "15M"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- inputs
sigSess  = input.session("0830-1400", "Signal hours (Chicago time)", tooltip="Tested best: 8:30 AM - 2:00 PM. Later signals often ran out of time before 3:40 PM.")
grades   = input.string("A+, A and B", "Grades to show (1M)", options=["A+ only", "A+ and A", "A+, A and B"])
abFrom   = input.string("11:00", "A and B only after (CT)", options=["any time", "10:00", "11:00", "12:00"], tooltip="A+ shows any time. Tested: 11:00 -> $6,512, any time -> $3,694, A+ only -> $2,348 (from $1,000 at 10% risk). 11:00 was picked after seeing the results.")
firstOnly = input.bool(true, "Only the first trade of the day", tooltip="Tested best. After the first signal whose limit fills, no more signals until the next day. A signal that never fills does not count. MES / MNQ / MYM share this (see the index setting below); gold has its own.")
acctBal  = input.float(1000, "Account balance ($)", minval=1, tooltip="Your whole account balance (all your charts share it, like the test). Update it after every trade - the test sized each trade from the balance at that moment.")
riskPct  = input.float(10, "Risk per trade (% of balance)", minval=0.1, maxval=100, tooltip="Tested: 10%. Contracts = 10% of the balance / what 1 contract loses at the stop, rounded down (skip if 1 contract is more), and no more contracts than the balance covers in day margin.")
showRR   = input.bool(true, "Draw entry / stop / target lines", tooltip="Lines with prices that follow the trade live until it ends (target, stop, 3:40 PM or limit cancelled), plus Filled / Target hit / Stopped markers.")
showPos  = input.bool(true, "Draw position tool (like TradingView's Long / Short Position)", tooltip="Green profit zone (entry to target) and red risk zone (entry to stop) with prices, ticks, $ and quantity. Follows the trade live until it ends.")
showWhy  = input.bool(true, "Mark the setup (15M level, push, CHoCH candle)")
showHalf = input.bool(false, "Draw +1R line (take half off, stop to breakeven)", tooltip="Off = full exit at the target, like the $6,512 test. Half off at 1R gave a smoother ride on the indices but less on gold.")
showCh   = input.bool(true, "Draw every CHoCH line", tooltip="Dashed line from the swing to the candle that closed through it, when the break flips direction. These are all changes of character, not just signals.")
showTbl  = input.bool(true, "Show status table")
grpOn    = input.bool(true, "One index trade a day across MES / MNQ / MYM", tooltip="Like the test: on an MES, MNQ or MYM chart, the indicator also checks the other two indices, and only the first index signal that fills each day is traded (ties: MES, then MNQ, then MYM). Gold (MGC) trades on its own.")
rrBox    = input.float(2.0, "Target (R)", minval=0.5, tooltip="2R tested best.")
maxWait  = input.int(10, "Cancel limit if not filled after (bars)", minval=1)
boxBars  = input.int(15, "+1R line length (bars)", minval=5)
minStop  = input.float(2.0, "Min stop (MES pts)", minval=0, tooltip="Scaled automatically on other markets.")
ptScIn   = input.float(0, "Point scale vs MES (0 = auto)", minval=0, tooltip="Auto: MES/ES 1, MNQ/NQ 6, MYM/YM 6.667, MGC/GC 0.667, M2K/RTY 0.44 (typical 1-minute candle size compared with MES, Sep - Oct 2026).")

riskUsd = acctBal * riskPct / 100
abMin   = abFrom == "10:00" ? 600 : abFrom == "11:00" ? 660 : abFrom == "12:00" ? 720 : 0

root    = syminfo.root
// day margin per contract and commission per contract round trip used in the test (micros)
margin  = (root == "MES" or root == "MYM") ? 50.0 : (root == "MNQ" or root == "MGC") ? 100.0 : na
comm    = 1.24
aPlus   = tfIdx == 0 ? 1.5 : 1.0                    // CHoCH candle body vs the average range
aMin    = 1.2
bMin    = 1.0
minDisp = tfIdx != 0 or grades == "A+ only" ? aPlus : grades == "A+ and A" ? aMin : bMin
approach = tfIdx == 0 ? 15 : 0                      // 1M: candles before the push that must not go past it
sweepBars = tfIdx == 0 ? 20 : tfIdx == 1 ? 6 : 4    // bars back to find the push into a level
lookDays = 3

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the signal (one function, so it can also run on the other indices)
// swing high/low of the candle two back, confirmed by the candle one back
f_piv() =>
    float ph = high[2] > high[3] and high[2] > high[1] ? high[2] : na
    float pl = low[2] < low[3] and low[2] < low[1] ? low[2] : na
    [ph, pl]

// market structure: bullish after a close above the latest swing high, bearish after a close below the latest swing low
f_struct() =>
    var int st = 0
    var float sh = na
    var float sl = na
    if high[1] > high[2] and high[1] >= high
        sh := high[1]
    if low[1] < low[2] and low[1] <= low
        sl := low[1]
    if not na(sh) and close > sh
        st := 1
    else if not na(sl) and close < sl
        st := -1
    st[1]

// Every valid signal on the symbol it runs on (on the chart, or through request.security on another index),
// before the one-trade-at-a-time and first-trade-of-the-day rules. Levels and trend are only used here, not drawn.
f_raw() =>
    sRoot = syminfo.root
    sc    = ptScIn > 0 ? ptScIn : (sRoot == "NQ" or sRoot == "MNQ") ? 6.0 : (sRoot == "YM" or sRoot == "MYM") ? 20.0 / 3 : (sRoot == "GC" or sRoot == "MGC") ? 2.0 / 3 : (sRoot == "RTY" or sRoot == "M2K") ? 0.44 : 1.0
    near  = (tfIdx == 0 ? 1.0 : tfIdx == 1 ? 3.0 : 4.0) * sc     // "at the level" = within this many points
    [pdh, pdl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
    [phH, plH] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htf, f_piv(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
    trend = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htf, f_struct(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
    // key levels - kind: 1 = higher-timeframe swing, 2 = prev day high/low
    var lvPx   = array.new_float()
    var lvKind = array.new_int()
    var lvT    = array.new_int()
    if timeframe.change(htf)
        if not na(phH)
            array.push(lvPx, phH)
            array.push(lvKind, 1)
            array.push(lvT, time)
        if not na(plH)
            array.push(lvPx, plH)
            array.push(lvKind, 1)
            array.push(lvT, time)
    if timeframe.change("D")
        if not na(pdh)
            array.push(lvPx, pdh)
            array.push(lvKind, 2)
            array.push(lvT, time)
        if not na(pdl)
            array.push(lvPx, pdl)
            array.push(lvKind, 2)
            array.push(lvT, time)
    lookMs = lookDays * 86400000
    while array.size(lvT) > 0 and time - array.get(lvT, 0) > lookMs + 86400000
        array.shift(lvPx)
        array.shift(lvKind)
        array.shift(lvT)
    // last swing high / low on this timeframe
    var float sH = na
    var float sL = na
    if high[1] > high[2] and high[1] >= high
        sH := high[1]
    if low[1] < low[2] and low[1] <= low
        sL := low[1]
    avgR = ta.sma(high - low, 30)[1]
    loO  = -ta.lowestbars(low, sweepBars + 1)
    hiO  = -ta.highestbars(high, sweepBars + 1)
    bull = not na(sH) and close[1] > sH and close[1] > open[1] and low > high[2]
    bear = not bull and not na(sL) and close[1] < sL and close[1] < open[1] and high < low[2]
    sd   = bull ? 1 : bear ? -1 : 0
    inS  = not na(time(timeframe.period, sigSess, "America/Chicago"))
    cMin = hour(time, "America/Chicago") * 60 + minute(time, "America/Chicago") + tfSec / 60
    int    rs = 0
    string rg = ""
    float  re = na
    float  rst = na
    float  rt = na
    float  rp = na
    int    ro = 0
    float  rx = na
    float  rl = na
    if sd != 0 and trend * sd > 0 and inS and not na(avgR) and bar_index > sweepBars + approach + 3
        disp    = math.abs(close[1] - open[1]) / avgR
        grade   = disp >= aPlus ? "A+" : disp >= aMin ? "A" : "B"
        if disp >= minDisp and (grade == "A+" or cMin >= abMin)
            off  = sd == 1 ? loO : hiO
            ext  = sd == 1 ? low[off] : high[off]
            extT = time[off]
            bool at15 = false
            bool atPD = false
            float lvl = na
            n = array.size(lvPx)
            if n > 0
                for j = 0 to n - 1
                    t0 = array.get(lvT, j)
                    if t0 <= extT and extT - t0 <= lookMs and math.abs(array.get(lvPx, j) - ext) <= near
                        if array.get(lvKind, j) == 1
                            at15 := true
                            if na(lvl) or math.abs(array.get(lvPx, j) - ext) < math.abs(lvl - ext)
                                lvl := array.get(lvPx, j)
                        else
                            atPD := true
            // 1M: price must have come INTO the level - none of the candles before the push went past it
            bool intoLevel = true
            if approach > 0
                for b = off + 1 to off + approach
                    if sd == 1 ? low[b] < ext : high[b] > ext
                        intoLevel := false
            if at15 and not atPD and intoLevel
                tick  = syminfo.mintick
                entry = sd == 1 ? math.floor((low + high[2]) / 2 / tick) * tick : math.ceil((high + low[2]) / 2 / tick) * tick
                sp    = math.max(math.abs(entry - (ext - sd * tick)), minStop * sc)
                rs  := sd
                rg  := grade
                re  := entry
                rst := entry - sd * sp
                rt  := entry + sd * sp * rrBox
                rp  := sp
                ro  := off
                rx  := ext
                rl  := lvl
    [rs, rg, re, rst, rt, rp, ro, rx, rl, trend, open, high, low]

[rSide, rGrade, rEntry, rStop, rTgt, rStopPts, rOff, rExt, rLvl, trd, oO, oH, oL] = f_raw()

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- change of character + fair-value gap on the chart's candles
var float swHi = na
var float swLo = na
var int   swHiBar = na
var int   swLoBar = na
var bool  hiUsed  = false
var bool  loUsed  = false
var int   lastBrk = 0        // direction of the last swing break: +1 up, -1 down
if high[1] > high[2] and high[1] >= high
    swHi    := high[1]
    swHiBar := bar_index - 1
    hiUsed  := false
if low[1] < low[2] and low[1] <= low
    swLo    := low[1]
    swLoBar := bar_index - 1
    loUsed  := false

// CHoCH line: a close through the last swing in the opposite direction to the previous break
if showCh and barstate.isconfirmed
    if not na(swHi) and not hiUsed and close > swHi
        hiUsed := true
        if lastBrk != 1
            line.new(swHiBar, swHi, bar_index, swHi, color=color.teal, width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
            label.new(math.round((swHiBar + bar_index) / 2), swHi, "CHoCH", style=label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor=color.teal, size=size.small)
        lastBrk := 1
    else if not na(swLo) and not loUsed and close < swLo
        loUsed := true
        if lastBrk != -1
            line.new(swLoBar, swLo, bar_index, swLo, color=color.red, width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
            label.new(math.round((swLoBar + bar_index) / 2), swLo, "CHoCH", style=label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor=color.red, size=size.small)
        lastBrk := -1

volAvg = ta.sma(volume, 20)
relVolC = volAvg[2] > 0 ? volume[1] / volAvg[2] : na    // the CHoCH candle's volume vs the 20 candles before it
relVolNow = volAvg[1] > 0 ? volume / volAvg[1] : na
inSess = not na(time(timeframe.period, sigSess, "America/Chicago"))
ctMin  = hour(time, "America/Chicago") * 60 + minute(time, "America/Chicago")
closeMin = ctMin + tfSec / 60                        // minutes after midnight CT when this candle closes

int   sig      = 0      // +1 buy, -1 sell
float sigEntry = na
float sigStop  = na

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- follow the last signal like the backtest
// One trade at a time: a signal's limit is working (cancelled after maxWait candles, or if a candle opens past
// the stop), then the trade is open until stop, target or 3:40 PM CT. The first fill of the day ends the day.
var int    tSide   = 0
var float  tEntry  = na
var float  tStop   = na
var float  tTgt    = na
var int    tBar    = na
var bool   tFilled = false
var bool   dayDone = false
var string tGrade  = ""
var string lastRes = ""
var float  tQty    = na
var float  tFill   = na
var int    tFilledBar = na
var line   lnE = na
var line   lnS = na
var line   lnT = na
var label  lbE = na
var label  lbS = na
var label  lbT = na
var box    bxT = na
var box    bxS = na

minW  = 8      // minimum width of the position boxes, in candles
// TradingView's Long / Short Position colors
cWin  = color.rgb(8, 153, 129)
cLoss = color.rgb(242, 54, 69)
// position box look: res 2 = pending limit, 1 = target hit, -1 = stopped, 0 = live (filled) or never filled
f_boxLook(int res) =>
    bool pend = res == 2
    // too big for your risk (the test skipped these): gray, so it is clearly not a trade to take
    cW = tQty >= 1 ? cWin : color.gray
    cL = tQty >= 1 ? cLoss : color.gray
    box.set_border_style(bxT, pend ? line.style_dashed : line.style_solid)
    box.set_border_style(bxS, pend ? line.style_dashed : line.style_solid)
    box.set_border_color(bxT, color.new(cW, pend ? 40 : res == -1 ? 35 : 0))
    box.set_border_color(bxS, color.new(cL, pend ? 40 : res == 1 ? 35 : 0))
    box.set_bgcolor(bxT, color.new(cW, pend ? 85 : res == 1 ? 55 : res == -1 ? 82 : 75))
    box.set_bgcolor(bxS, color.new(cL, pend ? 85 : res == -1 ? 55 : res == 1 ? 82 : 75))

// trade report: one alert per event (filled, target, stop, closed, cancelled) as a JSON line, so the day's
// results can be logged from TradingView's alert log or a webhook and compared with the backtest
f_report(string ev, float px) =>
    r = ev == "filled" or ev == "cancelled" ? 0.0 : (px - tFill) * tSide / math.abs(tFill - tStop)
    alert('{"type":"choch_result","symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","tf":"' + timeframe.period + '","time":"' + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "America/Chicago") + '","grade":"' + tGrade + '","side":"' + (tSide == 1 ? "long" : "short") + '","event":"' + ev + '","entry":' + str.tostring(tEntry) + ',"stop":' + str.tostring(tStop) + ',"target":' + str.tostring(tTgt) + ',"fill":' + str.tostring(tFill) + ',"price":' + str.tostring(px) + ',"r":' + str.tostring(r, "#.##") + ',"qty":' + str.tostring(tQty) + ',"usd":' + str.tostring(ev == "filled" or ev == "cancelled" ? 0.0 : r * math.abs(tFill - tStop) * syminfo.pointvalue * tQty - comm * tQty, "#.##") + '}', alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// end of a trade: stop the lines here and mark what happened (res: 1 target, -1 stop, 0 other)
f_end(string what, color c, float px, int res, string ev) =>
    f_report(ev, px)
    // boxes and lines stay at least minW candles wide so a quick trade is still readable;
    // the result marker sits on the real exit candle
    xEnd = math.max(bar_index, (tFilled ? tFilledBar : tBar + 1) + minW)
    if showPos
        box.set_right(bxT, xEnd)
        box.set_right(bxS, xEnd)
        if tFilled
            f_boxLook(res)
        else
            // limit never filled: no position was ever on, gray it out
            box.set_border_color(bxT, color.new(color.gray, 40))
            box.set_border_color(bxS, color.new(color.gray, 40))
            box.set_bgcolor(bxT, color.new(color.gray, 85))
            box.set_bgcolor(bxS, color.new(color.gray, 85))
    if showRR
        line.set_x2(lnE, xEnd)
        line.set_x2(lnS, xEnd)
        line.set_x2(lnT, xEnd)
        label.set_x(lbE, xEnd)
        label.set_x(lbS, xEnd)
        label.set_x(lbT, xEnd)
        label.new(bar_index, px, what, style=label.style_label_left, color=c, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
if timeframe.change("D")
    dayDone := false
    lastRes := ""
if tSide != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index > tBar
    if ctMin >= 15 * 60 + 40
        lastRes := tFilled ? "closed at 3:40 PM" : "limit not filled"
        px340 = open - tSide * syminfo.mintick
        f_end(tFilled ? "Closed 3:40 PM " + str.tostring((px340 - tFill) * tSide / math.abs(tFill - tStop), "+#.##;-#.##") + "R" : "Not filled", color.gray, px340, 0, tFilled ? "closed_340" : "cancelled")
        tSide := 0
    else
        if not tFilled
            if bar_index - tBar > maxWait or (tSide == 1 ? open <= tStop : open >= tStop)
                lastRes := "limit cancelled (not filled)"
                f_end("Cancelled: not filled", color.gray, tEntry, 0, "cancelled")
                tSide := 0
            else if (tSide == 1 ? low <= tEntry : high >= tEntry)
                tFilled := true
                dayDone := true
                tFilledBar := bar_index
                tFill   := (tSide == 1 ? open < tEntry : open > tEntry) ? open : tEntry
                if tFill != tEntry
                    // opened past the limit: filled at the open, target re-measured from the real fill
                    tTgt := tFill + tSide * rrBox * math.abs(tFill - tStop)
                    if showRR
                        line.set_y1(lnT, tTgt)
                        line.set_y2(lnT, tTgt)
                        label.set_y(lbT, tTgt)
                    if showPos
                        if tSide == 1
                            box.set_top(bxT, tTgt)
                        else
                            box.set_bottom(bxT, tTgt)
                // the position starts at the fill, like placing TradingView's position tool on the entry candle
                if showPos
                    box.set_left(bxT, bar_index)
                    box.set_left(bxS, bar_index)
                    f_boxLook(0)
                f_report("filled", tFill)
                label.new(bar_index, tFill, "Filled", style=tSide == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.blue, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        if tFilled and tSide != 0
            if tSide == 1 ? low <= tStop : high >= tStop
                lastRes := "stopped out"
                // 1 tick slippage; a candle (after the fill candle) that opens past the stop fills at its open
                gapS  = (tSide == 1 ? open < tStop : open > tStop) and not (bar_index == tFilledBar)
                pxS   = (gapS ? open : tStop) - tSide * syminfo.mintick
                f_end("Stopped " + str.tostring((pxS - tFill) * tSide / math.abs(tFill - tStop), "+#.##;-#.##") + "R", cLoss, pxS, -1, "stop")
                tSide := 0
            else if tSide == 1 ? high >= tTgt : low <= tTgt
                lastRes := "target hit"
                f_end("Target hit +" + str.tostring(rrBox) + "R", cWin, tTgt, 1, "target")
                tSide := 0
// keep the drawings running to the latest candle while the trade is working (at least minW candles wide)
xLive = math.max(bar_index + 3, (tFilled ? tFilledBar : tBar + 1) + minW)
if tSide != 0 and showPos
    box.set_right(bxT, xLive)
    box.set_right(bxS, xLive)
if tSide != 0 and showRR
    line.set_x2(lnE, xLive)
    line.set_x2(lnS, xLive)
    line.set_x2(lnT, xLive)
    label.set_x(lbE, xLive)
    label.set_x(lbS, xLive)
    label.set_x(lbT, xLive)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- one index trade a day (MES / MNQ / MYM together)
// Like the test: the indices share one first-trade-of-the-day. Each index chart runs the same signal on all three
// and follows them as one group: while one index's limit is working or its trade is open, other index signals are
// ignored; the first index fill ends the index day (even if it was too big for your risk and you skipped it).
// Ties on the same candle go to MES, then MNQ, then MYM. Gold (MGC) and other symbols are not grouped.
ownK = root == "MES" ? 0 : root == "MNQ" ? 1 : root == "MYM" ? 2 : -1
grp  = grpOn and ownK >= 0
[aS, aG, aE, aSt, aT, aP, aOff, aX, aLv, aTr, aO, aH, aL] = request.security("CME_MINI:MES1!", timeframe.period, f_raw(), gaps=barmerge.gaps_on)
[bS, bG, bE, bSt, bT, bP, bOff, bX, bLv, bTr, bO, bH, bL] = request.security("CME_MINI:MNQ1!", timeframe.period, f_raw(), gaps=barmerge.gaps_on)
[cS, cG, cE, cSt, cT, cP, cOff, cX, cLv, cTr, cO, cH, cL] = request.security("CBOT_MINI:MYM1!", timeframe.period, f_raw(), gaps=barmerge.gaps_on)
f_k(int k, float a, float b, float c) =>
    k == 0 ? a : k == 1 ? b : c
gName = array.from("MES", "MNQ", "MYM")
var int   gK      = -1        // index in the group whose signal is working / open (-1 = none)
var int   gSide   = 0
var int   gBar    = na
var float gE      = na
var float gS      = na
var float gT      = na
var bool  gFilled = false
var bool  gDone   = false
var int   gFirst  = -1        // which index filled first today
if timeframe.change("D")
    gDone  := false
    gFirst := -1
if grp and barstate.isconfirmed and gK >= 0 and bar_index > gBar
    o = f_k(gK, aO, bO, cO)
    h = f_k(gK, aH, bH, cH)
    l = f_k(gK, aL, bL, cL)
    if not na(o)
        if ctMin >= 15 * 60 + 40
            gK := -1
        else
            if not gFilled
                if bar_index - gBar > maxWait or (gSide == 1 ? o <= gS : o >= gS)
                    gK := -1
                else if (gSide == 1 ? l <= gE : h >= gE)
                    gFilled := true
                    gDone   := true
                    gFirst  := gK
                    f = (gSide == 1 ? o < gE : o > gE) ? o : gE
                    gT := f + gSide * rrBox * math.abs(f - gS)
                    if gK != ownK
                        label.new(bar_index, gSide == 1 ? low : high, array.get(gName, gK) + " filled: today's index trade,\nno more index trades here today", style=gSide == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.gray, 30), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
            if gFilled and gK >= 0
                if gSide == 1 ? l <= gS : h >= gS
                    gK := -1
                else if gSide == 1 ? h >= gT : l <= gT
                    gK := -1
int gPick = -1                // the index whose signal the group takes on this candle
if grp and barstate.isconfirmed and gK == -1 and not (firstOnly and gDone)
    for k = 0 to 2
        sk = k == 0 ? aS : k == 1 ? bS : cS
        if not na(sk) and sk != 0
            gPick   := k
            gK      := k
            gSide   := sk
            gBar    := bar_index
            gE      := f_k(k, aE, bE, cE)
            gS      := f_k(k, aSt, bSt, cSt)
            gT      := f_k(k, aT, bT, cT)
            gFilled := false
            break

// barstate.isconfirmed: only signal once the candle has closed, like the backtest
canSig = tSide == 0 and not (firstOnly and dayDone)
// with the index group on, this chart's signal is only traded if the group picked it (see above)
if canSig and rSide != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed and (not grp or gPick == ownK)
    side    = rSide
    grade   = rGrade
    off     = rOff
    ext     = rExt
    lvl     = rLvl
    tick    = syminfo.mintick
    entry   = rEntry
    stopPts = rStopPts
    stop    = rStop
    tgt     = rTgt
    sig      := side
    sigEntry := entry
    sigStop  := stop
    tSide   := side
    tEntry  := entry
    tStop   := stop
    tTgt    := tgt
    tBar    := bar_index
    tFilled := false
    tGrade  := grade
    stopTk  = math.round(stopPts / tick)
    perCtr  = stopPts * syminfo.pointvalue
    qty     = math.min(math.floor(riskUsd / perCtr), na(margin) ? 1000000 : math.floor(acctBal / margin))
    tQty    := qty
    sizeTxt = qty >= 1 ? str.tostring(qty) + " contracts = $" + str.tostring(qty * perCtr, "#") + " risk" : "1 contract risks $" + str.tostring(perCtr, "#") + " (more than your $" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#") + "): skip"
    volTxt  = na(relVolC) ? "" : "\nCHoCH volume " + str.tostring(relVolC, "#.#") + "x avg"
    txt = grade + " " + (side == 1 ? "BUY" : "SELL") + "\nlimit " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + "\nstop " + str.tostring(stop, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(stopTk) + " ticks)" + "\ntarget " + str.tostring(tgt, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(math.round(stopTk * rrBox)) + " ticks)" + "\n" + sizeTxt + volTxt
    fade = grade == "A+" ? 0 : grade == "A" ? 30 : 55
    // label on the far side of the candle from the limit (below for a short, above for a long) so the entry stays visible
    label.new(bar_index, side == 1 ? high : low, txt, style=side == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(side == 1 ? cWin : cLoss, fade), textcolor=color.white, size=size.normal)
    if showRR
        lnE := line.new(bar_index, entry, bar_index + 1 + minW, entry, color=color.blue, width=2)
        lnS := line.new(bar_index, stop, bar_index + 1 + minW, stop, color=cLoss, width=2)
        lnT := line.new(bar_index, tgt, bar_index + 1 + minW, tgt, color=cWin, width=2)
        qtyTxt = qty >= 1 ? " x" + str.tostring(qty) : ""
        lbE := label.new(bar_index + 1 + minW, entry, "Entry " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + qtyTxt, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.blue, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        lbS := label.new(bar_index + 1 + minW, stop, "Stop " + str.tostring(stop, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(stopTk) + " ticks)", style=label.style_label_left, color=cLoss, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        lbT := label.new(bar_index + 1 + minW, tgt, "Target " + str.tostring(rrBox) + "R " + str.tostring(tgt, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(math.round(stopTk * rrBox)) + " ticks)", style=label.style_label_left, color=cWin, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    if showPos
        ctrs   = math.max(qty, 1)
        tgtTxt = (qty < 1 ? "SKIP: 1 contract risks $" + str.tostring(perCtr, "#") + ", more than " + str.tostring(riskPct) + "% ($" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#") + ")\n" : "") + (side == 1 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + grade + "  ·  qty " + str.tostring(ctrs) + "  ·  R:R " + str.tostring(rrBox) + "\nTarget " + str.tostring(tgt, format.mintick) + "  (" + str.tostring(math.round(stopTk * rrBox)) + " ticks)  +$" + str.tostring(ctrs * (perCtr * rrBox - comm), "#")
        stpTxt = "Stop " + str.tostring(stop, format.mintick) + "  (" + str.tostring(stopTk) + " ticks)  -$" + str.tostring(ctrs * (perCtr + syminfo.mintick * syminfo.pointvalue + comm), "#") + "\nEntry " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + " (limit)"
        // starts on the next candle (the first one the limit can fill on), dashed until filled
        bxT := box.new(bar_index + 1, math.max(entry, tgt), bar_index + 1 + minW, math.min(entry, tgt), text=tgtTxt, text_size=size.small, text_color=color.white, text_halign=text.align_left, text_valign=side == 1 ? text.align_top : text.align_bottom)
        bxS := box.new(bar_index + 1, math.max(entry, stop), bar_index + 1 + minW, math.min(entry, stop), text=stpTxt, text_size=size.small, text_color=color.white, text_halign=text.align_left, text_valign=side == 1 ? text.align_bottom : text.align_top)
        f_boxLook(2)
    if showWhy
        if not na(lvl)
            line.new(bar_index - off - 20, lvl, bar_index + 3, lvl, color=color.orange, width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
            label.new(bar_index - off - 20, lvl, htfTxt + " level " + str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_right, color=color.new(color.orange, 20), textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny)
        label.new(bar_index - off, ext, "Push into level", style=side == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.orange, 100), textcolor=color.orange, size=size.small)
        label.new(bar_index - 1, side == 1 ? high[1] : low[1], "CHoCH", style=side == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    if showHalf
        r1 = entry + side * stopPts
        line.new(bar_index, r1, bar_index + boxBars, r1, color=color.yellow, width=1, style=line.style_dashed)
        label.new(bar_index + boxBars, r1, "+1R: take half, stop to BE", style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor=color.yellow, size=size.small)
    alert(grade + " " + (side == 1 ? "BUY " : "SELL ") + syminfo.ticker + ": limit " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + ", stop " + str.tostring(stop, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(stopTk) + " ticks), " + str.tostring(rrBox) + "R target " + str.tostring(tgt, format.mintick) + ", " + sizeTxt, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- status table (top right)
var table tbl = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 8, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 20), border_width=1, border_color=color.new(color.gray, 70))
f_row(int r, string k, string v, color c) =>
    table.cell(tbl, 0, r, k, text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, r, v, text_color=c, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
if showTbl and barstate.islast
    status = grp and gFirst >= 0 and gFirst != ownK and tSide == 0 ? "done for today (" + array.get(gName, gFirst) + " took the index trade)" : tSide != 0 and not tFilled ? tGrade + (tSide == 1 ? " BUY" : " SELL") + " limit working @ " + str.tostring(tEntry, format.mintick) : tSide != 0 ? tGrade + (tSide == 1 ? " LONG" : " SHORT") + " open, stop " + str.tostring(tStop, format.mintick) + ", target " + str.tostring(tTgt, format.mintick) : firstOnly and dayDone ? "done for today" + (lastRes != "" ? " (" + lastRes + ")" : "") : inSess ? "waiting for a setup" + (lastRes != "" ? " (last: " + lastRes + ")" : "") : "outside signal hours"
    stColor = tSide != 0 ? color.yellow : (firstOnly and dayDone) or (grp and gFirst >= 0) ? color.gray : color.white
    f_row(0, syminfo.ticker, timeframe.period + " min", color.white)
    f_row(1, htfTxt + " trend", trd == 1 ? "bullish (longs only)" : trd == -1 ? "bearish (shorts only)" : "none yet", trd == 1 ? color.teal : trd == -1 ? color.red : color.gray)
    f_row(2, "Volume (last candle)", na(relVolNow) ? "n/a" : str.tostring(relVolNow, "#.#") + "x 20-candle avg", relVolNow >= 1.5 ? color.orange : color.white)
    f_row(3, "Today", status, stColor)
    f_row(4, "A / B allowed", grades == "A+ only" or tfIdx != 0 ? "no (A+ only)" : closeMin >= abMin ? "yes" : "after " + abFrom, color.white)
    f_row(5, "Risk per trade", "$" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#") + " (" + str.tostring(riskPct) + "% of $" + str.tostring(acctBal, "#") + ")", color.white)
    f_row(6, "Max trades", firstOnly ? "first fill of the day" : "one at a time", color.white)
    gTxt = not grp ? (ownK >= 0 ? "off" : "not an index (trades on its own)") : gFirst >= 0 ? "done: " + array.get(gName, gFirst) + " filled first" + (gFirst == ownK ? " (this chart)" : "") : gK >= 0 ? array.get(gName, gK) + (gFilled ? " trade open" : " limit working") : "free - first index fill wins"
    f_row(7, "Index trade today", gTxt, grp and gFirst >= 0 and gFirst != ownK ? color.gray : color.white)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- data window + alerts
plot(sig, "Signal (+1 buy, -1 sell)", display=display.data_window)
plot(sigEntry, "Entry", display=display.data_window)
plot(sigStop, "Stop", display=display.data_window)
plot(relVolNow, "Volume vs 20-candle avg", display=display.data_window)

alertcondition(sig == 1, "BUY", "{{ticker}} BUY: limit {{plot(\"Entry\")}}, stop {{plot(\"Stop\")}}")
alertcondition(sig == -1, "SELL", "{{ticker}} SELL: limit {{plot(\"Entry\")}}, stop {{plot(\"Stop\")}}")

if barstate.islast and (not timeframe.isintraday or tfSec > 900)
    label.new(bar_index, high, "CHoCH Setups is built for 1, 5 or 15-minute charts", color=color.orange, textcolor=color.black)
if barstate.islast and not (root == "MES" or root == "MNQ" or root == "MYM" or root == "MGC")
    label.new(bar_index, low, "Tested on MES1!, MNQ1!, MYM1! and MGC1! futures only.\n" + syminfo.ticker + ": point scale, ticks and contract sizes may be wrong.", style=label.style_label_up, color=color.orange, textcolor=color.black)
